invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: widemul_poly1305_ifma reads CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA alone, so a session
  whose caller did not state CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY runs IFMA's
  52-bit products on its one-time key, which no statement covers. Every tag
  is still right. bin/x86_kernels_test counts the kernel's calls under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and the script builds it for x86-64, where widemul.h
  compiles the function.

--- old
    return widemul_native(widemul) && (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
--- new
    (void)widemul;
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
